    <statement><p>Find the equation in polar coordinates of the line
through the origin with slope <m>\frac1{4}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\theta=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.244979</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>m=\frac{1}{4}</m> makes an angle
<m>{\theta }_{0}={ \tan}^{-1}\frac{1}{4}\approx 0.24498</m> with the positive
<m>x</m>-axis.

 The equation of the line is
<m>\theta = 0.24498</m>, while
<m>r</m> is arbitrary.


</solution>
